+# Offline capture acceptance — bounded continuation, 2026-10-09
+
+Implement in existing observer-probe; no new engine, runtime, listeners or owner.
+Consume captured native Hermes metadata and caller-authored SourceEvent template.
+For fixture-only PRE_OBSERVER_SOURCE_CONTEXT / HISTORICAL_IMPORT capture, bind the
+source tuple (source_id, source_instance_id/generation, source_stream_id,
+sequence_epoch, native_event_id and structured position) durably to event_id UUIDv7.
+Verify template generation/session/row/locator/hash against captured metadata.
+Require separate fixture SERVICE_ACTOR writer provenance; never infer it from
+correlated actor or source reporter. No EvidenceEvent is emitted by acceptance.
+
+Primary recovery authority: locked append-only SHA256-sealed NDJSON journal,
+not a second ID map/index. Append/fdatasync before acknowledgment; fsync the new
+journal directory entry. Scan and verify accepted records on reopen; dedupe exact
+native occurrence tuple, reject changed request or writer rebinding. Incomplete
+last frame is an unaccepted tail and may be truncated; malformed complete frames
+fail closed. Recover/sync an intact unacknowledged frame before replay acknowledgment.
+Local observer_sequence satisfies journal writer provenance only, not global order.
+
+Inject process-exit points before write, midway through frame, after complete
+write/before sync and after sync/before reply. Check only accepted records, not
+whether a UUID was allocated in a failed attempt. Run serial and concurrent retry,
+reopen, distinct generation/epoch/equal bytes, changed source and corrupted journal
+regressions. Connect actual accepted source JSON to the existing Python reference
+roundtrip with artifact custody and additive correction. Preserve old checkpoints.
+
+No live writer authority is created. Fixture actor/receipt requirements are input
+provenance tests, not production authorization. Exact journal encoding is open in
+Observer v0.2 section8; this uses that permitted seam. Canonical full production
+validation/authority, artifact capture, source coverage, OS power-loss/platform
+qualification and PostgreSQL deployment remain separate gaps.
